WEBVTT

00:00:04.790 --> 00:00:09.212
Simon Simple is at the station. He is going on a train.

00:00:09.272 --> 00:00:12.814
There are policemen at the station.

00:00:12.874 --> 00:00:16.486
There are policemen on the trains.

00:00:16.546 --> 00:00:20.458
They are all working very hard.

00:00:20.518 --> 00:00:23.450
“Why are the police here?”

00:00:23.510 --> 00:00:25.622
Simon asks a man.

00:00:25.682 --> 00:00:29.084
“Look,” the man says.

00:00:29.144 --> 00:00:32.884
Simon looks at the man's newspaper.

00:00:32.944 --> 00:00:35.534
“Do you know this man?”

00:00:35.594 --> 00:00:36.915
he reads.

00:00:36.974 --> 00:00:39.326
“He’s a spy!”

00:00:39.386 --> 00:00:40.726
“Find him!”

00:00:40.786 --> 00:00:42.046
“Stop him!”

00:00:42.106 --> 00:00:44.068
“Catch him!”

00:00:44.128 --> 00:00:48.340
Simon looks at the people in the station.

00:00:48.400 --> 00:00:54.622
He can see students in jeans, and men in suits.

00:00:54.682 --> 00:00:58.364
He can see families and children.

00:00:58.424 --> 00:01:01.860
He cannot see any spies.

00:01:01.920 --> 00:01:08.698
Simon’s train goes at 11.00, and it is 10.57 now.

00:01:08.758 --> 00:01:11.680
Simon runs to the train.

00:01:11.740 --> 00:01:16.164
There is an old woman with an umbrella near Simon.

00:01:16.224 --> 00:01:19.286
She is walking very fast.

00:01:19.346 --> 00:01:21.718
Simon does not see her.

00:01:21.778 --> 00:01:24.230
He does not see her bag.

00:01:24.289 --> 00:01:28.182
The old woman's bag hits Simon's foot.

00:01:28.242 --> 00:01:30.494
Simon falls.

00:01:30.554 --> 00:01:32.909
His bag opens.

00:01:32.969 --> 00:01:36.234
His things fall to the ground.

00:01:36.294 --> 00:01:39.946
The old woman’s bag is open, too.

00:01:40.006 --> 00:01:42.787
A letter falls out.

00:01:42.847 --> 00:01:46.549
Simon puts his things into his bag.

00:01:46.609 --> 00:01:50.722
The old woman's letter is with Simon's things.

00:01:50.782 --> 00:01:53.422
Simon does not see it.

00:01:53.482 --> 00:01:57.434
He puts the old woman's letter in his bag.

00:01:57.494 --> 00:02:01.627
He closes his bag, and runs to the train.

00:02:01.687 --> 00:02:04.669
Simon sits down in the train.

00:02:04.728 --> 00:02:08.432
There is a beautiful girl beside him.

00:02:08.492 --> 00:02:11.604
“Hello,” Simon says.

00:02:11.664 --> 00:02:14.976
“Hello,” the girl says.

00:02:15.035 --> 00:02:18.578
The old woman is on the train, too.

00:02:18.638 --> 00:02:22.350
She is looking at Simon’s bag.

00:02:22.410 --> 00:02:25.612
She wants her letter.

00:02:25.672 --> 00:02:28.794
There are policemen on the train.

00:02:28.854 --> 00:02:31.880
They cannot find the spy.

00:02:31.939 --> 00:02:35.254
The old woman sees the policemen.

00:02:35.314 --> 00:02:39.788
She turns and walks quickly down the train.

00:02:39.848 --> 00:02:42.460
Simon likes the girl.

00:02:42.520 --> 00:02:45.142
She likes him.

00:02:45.201 --> 00:02:48.304
“There’s a restaurant on the train,”

00:02:48.364 --> 00:02:49.405
Simon says.

00:02:49.425 --> 00:02:53.138
“Do you want a cup of coffee?”

00:02:53.198 --> 00:02:54.948
“Yes, please,”

00:02:55.008 --> 00:02:56.470
The girl says.

00:02:56.529 --> 00:02:57.690
“OK,

00:02:57.750 --> 00:02:58.881
wait here,”

00:02:58.941 --> 00:03:01.416
Simon says.

00:03:01.476 --> 00:03:06.152
Simon takes his bag and goes to the restaurant.

00:03:06.212 --> 00:03:09.454
The old woman is waiting for him.

00:03:09.514 --> 00:03:12.095
Simon does not see her.

00:03:12.155 --> 00:03:15.796
He does not see her foot.

00:03:15.856 --> 00:03:19.438
The train is going fast.

00:03:19.498 --> 00:03:21.539
Simon falls.

00:03:21.599 --> 00:03:24.500
The old woman falls, too.

00:03:24.560 --> 00:03:27.812
She sits down on the floor.

00:03:27.872 --> 00:03:30.432
“Oh, I’m sorry,”

00:03:30.492 --> 00:03:31.818
Simon says.

00:03:31.878 --> 00:03:34.384
He helps the old woman.

00:03:34.444 --> 00:03:38.758
Simon sees the old woman's shoes.

00:03:38.818 --> 00:03:44.162
He looks at her shoes, and he looks at her face.

00:03:44.222 --> 00:03:47.275
“They’re not women’s shoes,”

00:03:47.334 --> 00:03:49.366
Simon thinks.

00:03:49.426 --> 00:03:54.140
Simon buys the coffee, and goes back to the girl.

00:03:54.200 --> 00:03:56.802
The train stops.

00:03:56.862 --> 00:04:01.584
Simon and the girl are going on a boat now.

00:04:01.644 --> 00:04:05.404
They walk from the train to the boat.

00:04:05.464 --> 00:04:08.805
There are policemen here, too.

00:04:08.865 --> 00:04:11.116
“What do they want?”

00:04:11.176 --> 00:04:12.897
The girl asks.

00:04:12.957 --> 00:04:14.928
“There’s a spy,”

00:04:14.987 --> 00:04:16.718
Simon says.

00:04:16.778 --> 00:04:18.490
“A spy?”

00:04:18.549 --> 00:04:20.420
The girl says.

00:04:20.480 --> 00:04:23.252
“I can’t see any spies.”

00:04:23.311 --> 00:04:25.773
Simon looks too.

00:04:25.832 --> 00:04:29.304
He sees families and students.

00:04:29.364 --> 00:04:31.617
He sees the old woman.

00:04:31.677 --> 00:04:34.620
“No,” Simon says.

00:04:34.680 --> 00:04:38.173
“I can’t see any spies.”

00:04:38.233 --> 00:04:41.584
It is a beautiful day.

00:04:41.644 --> 00:04:45.818
The sun is shining and the water is blue.

00:04:45.878 --> 00:04:51.480
Simon and the girl sit near the water and wait.

00:04:51.540 --> 00:04:53.542
The boat is coming.

00:04:53.602 --> 00:04:55.913
“What’s your name?”

00:04:55.973 --> 00:04:57.644
Simon asks.

00:04:57.704 --> 00:04:59.305
“Samantha,”

00:04:59.365 --> 00:05:01.153
The girl says.

00:05:01.213 --> 00:05:04.261
“Oh,” Simon says.

00:05:04.321 --> 00:05:06.521
“My name’s Simon.

00:05:06.581 --> 00:05:09.282
Simon and Samantha.

00:05:09.342 --> 00:05:11.343
That’s nice.”

00:05:11.402 --> 00:05:14.894
Simon and Samantha are talking.

00:05:14.953 --> 00:05:17.944
They do not see the old woman.

00:05:18.004 --> 00:05:21.706
They do not see her umbrella.

00:05:21.766 --> 00:05:24.196
“Look out!”

00:05:24.256 --> 00:05:25.946
A man shouts.

00:05:26.006 --> 00:05:28.317
“There’s a lorry!”

00:05:28.377 --> 00:05:31.588
Simon and Samantha look.

00:05:31.648 --> 00:05:35.518
A lorry is coming down the road very fast.

00:05:35.578 --> 00:05:39.470
They jump back.

00:05:39.530 --> 00:05:44.564
The old woman jumps back, too.

00:05:44.624 --> 00:05:48.415
Simon sees her trousers.

00:05:48.475 --> 00:05:51.586
“They’re not women’s trousers,”

00:05:51.646 --> 00:05:53.528
Simon thinks.

00:05:53.588 --> 00:05:55.478
“Come on, Simon,

00:05:55.538 --> 00:05:56.979
the boat’s here,”

00:05:57.039 --> 00:05:58.958
Samantha says.

00:05:59.018 --> 00:06:02.758
Simon and Samantha get on the boat.

00:06:02.818 --> 00:06:07.590
Simon opens his bag and takes his lunch out.

00:06:07.650 --> 00:06:13.542
He takes the old woman’s letter out, too, but he does not see it.

00:06:13.602 --> 00:06:16.142
“Do you want a sandwich?”

00:06:16.202 --> 00:06:18.533
Simon asks Samantha.

00:06:18.593 --> 00:06:20.244
“Yes, please,”

00:06:20.304 --> 00:06:22.184
Samantha says.

00:06:22.244 --> 00:06:25.695
She takes her lunch out of her bag.

00:06:25.755 --> 00:06:27.636
“Do you want an apple?”

00:06:27.696 --> 00:06:29.044
She says.

00:06:29.104 --> 00:06:32.064
The old woman is behind them.

00:06:32.124 --> 00:06:35.706
Simon and Samantha do not see her.

00:06:35.766 --> 00:06:38.377
They do not see her hand.

00:06:38.437 --> 00:06:41.298
The boat is going fast now.

00:06:41.358 --> 00:06:44.220
The wind is strong.

00:06:44.280 --> 00:06:47.841
Samantha's hair goes in her eyes.

00:06:47.901 --> 00:06:51.382
The wind takes the old woman's letter.

00:06:51.442 --> 00:06:54.984
The letter flies along the boat.

00:06:55.044 --> 00:06:57.216
“What’s that paper?”

00:06:57.275 --> 00:06:59.014
Samantha says.

00:06:59.074 --> 00:07:01.504
“Is it your boat ticket?”

00:07:01.564 --> 00:07:03.285
“I don’t know,”

00:07:03.345 --> 00:07:05.006
Simon says.

00:07:05.066 --> 00:07:06.786
Simon runs.

00:07:06.846 --> 00:07:08.708
He wants his ticket.

00:07:08.768 --> 00:07:11.238
The old woman runs, too.

00:07:11.298 --> 00:07:13.710
She wants her letter.

00:07:13.770 --> 00:07:17.602
Simon and the old woman run fast.

00:07:17.662 --> 00:07:21.264
They are near the paper now.

00:07:21.323 --> 00:07:24.435
“Woof!” What is that?

00:07:24.495 --> 00:07:26.136
It is a dog!

00:07:26.196 --> 00:07:28.624
He is running very fast.

00:07:28.684 --> 00:07:33.352
He runs to the paper and catches it in his mouth.

00:07:33.412 --> 00:07:35.203
“My ticket!”

00:07:35.263 --> 00:07:36.904
Simon says.

00:07:36.964 --> 00:07:39.255
“My letter!”

00:07:39.315 --> 00:07:41.336
The old woman says.

00:07:41.396 --> 00:07:44.378
The dog runs along the boat.

00:07:44.438 --> 00:07:46.249
“Catch the dog!”

00:07:46.308 --> 00:07:47.870
Simon says.

00:07:47.929 --> 00:07:49.751
“Stop him!”

00:07:49.810 --> 00:07:51.501
Says the old woman.

00:07:51.561 --> 00:07:53.462
The dog is happy.

00:07:53.522 --> 00:07:55.503
He can run fast.

00:07:55.563 --> 00:07:59.374
He is playing a game with Simon and the old woman.

00:07:59.434 --> 00:08:02.106
He does not see Samantha.

00:08:02.166 --> 00:08:05.567
Samantha jumps up and catches him.

00:08:05.627 --> 00:08:07.538
“I’ve got him, Simon,”

00:08:07.598 --> 00:08:09.548
Samantha says.

00:08:09.608 --> 00:08:13.650
Simon and the old woman run to Samantha.

00:08:13.710 --> 00:08:16.552
The paper is in the dog’s mouth.

00:08:16.612 --> 00:08:18.762
Simon looks at it.

00:08:18.822 --> 00:08:21.713
“That’s not my ticket,” he says.

00:08:21.733 --> 00:08:22.802
“No,”

00:08:22.862 --> 00:08:27.042
the old woman says. “It’s my letter.”

00:08:27.102 --> 00:08:33.054
The dog likes Simon and Samantha, but he does not like the old woman.

00:08:33.114 --> 00:08:37.126
He takes her coat in his mouth and pulls it.

00:08:37.186 --> 00:08:39.798
The coat falls to the ground.

00:08:39.858 --> 00:08:42.980
The wind takes the old woman's hat.

00:08:43.040 --> 00:08:45.331
It falls into the water.

00:08:45.391 --> 00:08:48.222
Her hair falls with the hat.

00:08:48.282 --> 00:08:52.030
Simon and Samantha look at the old woman.

00:08:52.090 --> 00:08:54.288
It is not an old woman!

00:08:54.348 --> 00:08:56.260
It is a man!

00:08:56.320 --> 00:08:58.612
“The spy!”

00:08:58.672 --> 00:09:00.352
Simon says.

00:09:00.412 --> 00:09:04.506
“Police! Come here!”

00:09:04.565 --> 00:09:09.059
The police are very happy.

00:09:09.119 --> 00:09:11.510
“Thank you, Simon,”

00:09:11.570 --> 00:09:12.982
They say.

00:09:13.042 --> 00:09:16.104
“Now we have the spy.

00:09:16.164 --> 00:09:19.062
But the spy has a letter.

00:09:19.122 --> 00:09:23.119
The letter has names and addresses on it.

00:09:23.179 --> 00:09:27.470
We want the letter but we can’t find it.

00:09:27.530 --> 00:09:29.140
Where is it?

00:09:29.200 --> 00:09:31.111
Do you know?”

00:09:31.171 --> 00:09:33.912
Simon looks at the dog.

00:09:33.972 --> 00:09:36.812
The dog looks at Simon.

00:09:36.872 --> 00:09:38.863
“There’s the letter,”

00:09:38.923 --> 00:09:40.723
Simon says.

00:09:40.783 --> 00:09:42.233
“Where?”

00:09:42.294 --> 00:09:44.234
Says the policeman.

00:09:44.294 --> 00:09:46.675
“It’s in the dog,”

00:09:46.735 --> 00:09:48.492
Simon says.

00:09:48.552 --> 00:09:49.330
Ugh!